## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of timer interrupts, context switches, and simple schedulers at kernel level. It also probes how aging prevents starvation.

## Key Concepts
- Preemptive scheduling and round-robin
- Timer interrupt handling and context-switch protocol
- Per-process state and a ready-queue data structure
- Aging to prevent starvation under load

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-kernel RR tick
function timerTick(running, ready) {
  running.quantum--;
  if (running.quantum <= 0) {
    ready.enqueue(running);
    const next = ready.dequeue();
    contextSwitch(running, next);
  }
}
```

